      "created": "2022-07-22T12:46:34.264Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [
        {
          "_id": "5a995d0bbf71f62789f7311d",
          "alias": "Zircon blue Chameleon",
          "aliasID": "65c2d3d2ed6eefce4cafc83d",
          "anonymized": false,
          "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/c70b7d92af598db0ef814ab09309a86e.png",
          "created": "2018-03-02T14:17:47.571Z",
          "name": "Sophie123p",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": null
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "62d9a82781ce915b21189dd1",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62d63ae34cc04b44a26825a5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a995d0bbf71f62789f7311d|full_name}: I appreciate the input! \nWhile at the core I would LOVE for everyone to be able to be fully shown all the time and, as you put it, \"seen for what they are\". That simply isn't the case these days.\nThe way ripperstore and other such clients work is actually through a modded client interpreting your catche data. Which is only accessable when a model is fully shown for the local user. \nThis system would allow for a person to control who gets to see or who doesn't get to see an avatar. In my post, I did suggest a setting that allows for a sort of \"blanket\" option such as an \"allow all\" button. \nNow, like any solution, this is not perfect. I will be the first to admit that. Any person you allow to see your avatar runs the risk of that person being a ripper of some sort. However, this would be a defensive barrier against that happening without the users input or force cloning. Simply suggesting that everyone either use a public avatar or make their avatars public to stop ripping would remove any and all individuality that this game has on an avatar level.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
