      "value": "@{5d100f3eb716313272a55e89|full_name}: The way RipperStore works is that once an avatar is fully shown, they can access that users cache and \"archive\" the avatar. If this system were to be implemented, this would help solve this issue by putting up a barrier between the local and remote user. Would this completely solve the issue? Not at all. Anyone you show the avatar with runs the risk of being a ripper, but at least at that point, you cannot be force ripped or cloned.",
